DTEND:20260927T210033Z
SUMMARY:(1246) Chaka hides a mag 10.3 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(1246) Chaka hides a magnitude 10.3 star\, seen from Rourkela.\
 nThe predicted edge passes 4 km to the NW\, so a miss is likely — but a 
 chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest
  approach 02:25:33 IST\, give or take 3 s. The star is 54° up in the NE 
 · dark sky.\nIt fades 4.7 magnitudes for up to 1.8 s on the centre line\,
  and the path is 18 km wide\, give or take 12 km.\nFinder chart\, the map 
 and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#2026-09-27
 -1246-chaka-461952
